SnipNova
========

This product is built on the open-source SupoClip project
(https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip), copyright its respective
contributors, and is distributed under the GNU Affero General Public
License v3.0 (see LICENSE).

SnipNova adds its own branding, interface design and features on top of
that upstream foundation. The SupoClip name is used in this notice only
to give the attribution the license requires.

The YouTube-captions transcript path (backend/src/media/yt_captions.py —
using the timed captions YouTube already serves as the word-timed
transcript instead of running a speech model) follows the approach of
NeonClipping, an MIT-licensed open-source project. The implementation
here is original; the idea is credited to NeonClipping's authors with
thanks, per the MIT licence's attribution spirit.

The word-timing alignment and caption-coverage check in
backend/src/media/word_align.py (snapping word edges onto the loudness
envelope, and verifying every speech block has a caption over it) are
adapted from wordcaps (https://github.com/Axeeh/wordcaps, commit
ff520f4), an MIT-licensed open-source project, © its authors. The MIT
licence permits this use with attribution, given here with thanks.

